  "findings": [
    "All 27 profiles01 frozen launch environments lack QR_PREFIX and SOLVER; the 18 launched execution records retain that absence. Nine warm dependents never launched.",
    "The four diagnostic04 environments and pilot04 environment inherit the same omission; controllers strip inherited ORBIT_POC_* variables before applying their recorded environment.",
    "The production backend sets QR_PREFIX and scaled_qr_v1 SOLVER in the process launch environment.",
    "The pinned native processing dispatcher invokes initParameter before the numerics processing step process() sets the QR environment. Its inherited expectInitializedParameters() is true.",
    "The pinned native enabled() predicate requires nonempty QR_PREFIX, so initial bias datum construction followed its legacy branches for these recorded launches. Subsequent profile QR activation does not rebuild the already initialized datum.",
    "No qr.datum.* records exist in the 18 launched profiles01 attempts, four diagnostic04 replays, or pilot04, consistent with the initialization path established by the pinned controls.",
    "The actual pilot04 error is the legacy code-bias datum eigen decomposition during initialization, before a completed QR profile. This does not establish a production QR path defect.",
    "The original 3 complete / 15 failed / 9 blocked outcomes and diagnostic first-difference signed-zero measurements remain preserved observations under the recorded harness. They do not establish production-backend warm-start behavior."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The environment/path conclusion combines frozen launch controls and pinned native source order; no new native instrumentation or execution was performed.",
    "This supplement does not prove that fixing the launch environment resolves signed-zero differences, activates nonzero code/TEC priors, or permits warm import.",
    "Corrected harness results require a new freeze and new attempts with prelaunch QR prefix/solver, datum evidence, unchanged scientific checks, and independent outcome review. Old artifacts must not be rewritten."
  ],
